{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION — 1305 does NOT make harness run 30840572608 diagnostic. I overstated it.\n\nI claimed (in 39c1's AC4 comment and in e369's HANDOFF #24) that 1305 would let the next harness run\ndistinguish the two readings of the parent no-op:\n\n> if DC is ERRORING on these writes and the swallow was hiding it, an alert will now appear; if no\n> alert appears, DC returned success and lied.\n\n**That is wrong, and it is wrong in the direction that would have let me read a false negative as\nevidence.** I checked before relying on it:\n\n    grep -rn \"bridge_alert\" tests/external/live_jira_dc/      -> nothing\n    grep -rn \"bridge_alerts\" .github/workflows/external-integration.yml -> nothing\n\nNo live cell reads the alert store, and no workflow step prints or uploads it. `record_parent_divergence`\nwrites to `<repo_root>/bridge_state/bridge_alerts/<date>.jsonl` inside the ephemeral runner's working\nrepo, which is destroyed when the job ends. The records are produced and then discarded unread.\n\nSo \"no alert appeared\" in run 30840572608 will mean **nothing was looked at**, not \"DC returned\nsuccess\". Had I not checked, the absence of alerts was exactly the kind of silence I would have been\ntempted to read as a signal — which is the same mistake, in miniature, that this epic keeps paying for.\n\n### What the run CAN and CANNOT settle\n\n**CAN** — whether the Epic Link path works. The parent cells read `fields.parent` (and the epic link)\nback over raw REST and compare against what was written. That is a direct observation and needs no\nalerting.\n\n**CANNOT** — whether a failed parent write ERRORED or was ACCEPTED-AND-IGNORED. That distinction is\n[rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda]'s first acceptance criterion, and it remains open after this run.\n\n### What 1305 is still worth\n\nIt is not wasted: in PRODUCTION the alert store is a real operator surface (`rebar` reads bridge\nalerts; `reads_cli._bridge_alert_warning` surfaces them), and 39c1's AC4 asks for an operator-visible\nsignal in a deployment, not for harness observability. The AC is met. What is missing is a separate\nthing — the harness has no window onto the alert store — and I have recorded that on 1a9f as the\nconcrete way to settle its AC1 rather than leaving it implied."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785781545451866001,"uuid":"ae2bfdfd-debc-4a28-956a-da15e790f06b"}